<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Casimir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1651">1651</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as New Amstel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Casimir was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fort built in 1651 on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delaware-river">Delaware River</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-stuyvesant">Peter Stuyvesant</a> to challenge the colony of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. The Swedes seized it in 1654 and renamed it Fort Trinity, prompting the Dutch to conquer all of New Sweden in 1655. Renamed New Amstel, it later passed to the English and became the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-castle-delaware">New Castle, Delaware</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-casimir.jpg" alt="Fort Casimir" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dedden 11:31, 30 April 2006 (UTC) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nieuw_Nederland.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
